  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tuberculosis Diagnostic Network Strengthening Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  USAID&apos;s Tuberculosis (TB) Diagnostic Network Strengthening activity enhances the capacity of government and private sector laboratory systems to diagnose TB cases through equitable, accessible, rapid, and quality-assured testing. Using FY 2024 funds, the activity will support standardizing procedures and practices to meet the global quality standards for TB test results. Moreover, the activity will improve the laboratory information management systems and implement an optimized and reliable specimen transportation plan. The activity will also collaborate with private diagnostic networks to ensure that TB patients diagnosed in private laboratories adhere to national guidelines, meet international standards, and report patients to the national reporting system. The activity will closely collaborate with the National Tuberculosis Control Program to improve timely and accurate TB diagnosis; link confirmed cases to treatment services; reduce the spread of TB and preventable deaths; and contribute to global TB targets. The activity will have nationwide coverage, with an emphasis on underserved sections of the healthcare system. The activity will support the Joint Strategic Plan Goal Three, with the U.S. government&apos;s Integrated Country Strategy Mission Objective of Improving inclusive and equitable health, education, and livelihood services, especially for women, youth, and marginalized groups. The activity will advance the Indo-Pacific Strategy by working with GoB to intensify efforts to prevent, detect, and respond to infectious diseases.FY 2024 funding will contribute to SL Indirect ($700k), Digital Technology-Indirect ($250k), Innovation ($100k) Gender Equality ($500k), Health Workforce ($400k), PGI-Indirect Digital ($1.25m),PGI-Indirect Health ($1.45m) and PSE ($100k) issues.</narrative>
  </description>
